sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client · POST /bff/checkout
    participant R as FedGQL Router
    participant K as checkout subgraph · orchestrator
    participant CT as cart subgraph
    participant I as inventory subgraph
    participant P as payments subgraph
    C->>R: mutation SubmitCheckout(input: cartId, paymentMethodId, shippingAddress)
    R->>K: submitCheckout(input)
    Note over K: saga / process coordinator — steps run inside the resolver (internal gRPC or HTTP), not through the router
    K->>CT: 1. cart(id) — lines + totalAmount
    CT-->>K: Cart
    K->>I: 2. inventory(sku, storeId) per line
    I-->>K: Inventory (availableToSell)
    Note over K: 3. create a pending Order
    K->>P: 4. processPayment(input: amount, currency, paymentMethodId, referenceId = order id)
    P-->>K: PaymentTransaction (SUCCESS / DECLINED)
    K->>CT: 5. clearCart(input: cartId)
    CT-->>K: Cart (empty)
    Note over K: on failure after a write, compensate (refund / restore the cart) and return success false
    K-->>R: CheckoutResult { success, order, errors }
    R-->>C: { data: { submitCheckout } } — Order status and payment transaction
